{"seq":6,"slug":"theodore-roosevelt-legacy","title":"西奥多·罗斯福：历史影响与评价","stage":"DONE","category":"theodore-roosevelt","categoryLabel":"西奥多·罗斯福","chapterCount":3,"docCount":8,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy","rating":{"composite":3.62,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":2.5,"positioning":null,"strategic":5},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/leaders/10_theodore-roosevelt/6_theodore-roosevelt-legacy","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"西奥多-罗斯福-历史影响与评价\">西奥多·罗斯福：历史影响与评价</h1><p>1919 年 1 月罗斯福在睡梦中辞世时，年仅六十岁。副总统马歇尔的悼词流传至今：&quot;死神必须趁他睡着才敢带走西奥多·罗斯福——若他醒着，必有一场恶斗。&quot;这句半带戏谑的话，恰好点出了后世评价这位第二十六任总统时反复出现的张力：他是一股几乎无法被驯服的能量，既留下了深远的建设性遗产，也留下了至今争论不休的难题。</p>\n<p>本系列不再复述罗斯福&quot;做了什么&quot;——那属于前几个分卷（生平、崛起、进步主义改革、外交、自然保护）的范畴。这一卷专门处理一个更难的问题：在他离世一个多世纪之后，他到底&quot;意味着什么&quot;？我们今天为何仍把他的头像刻在拉什莫尔山上，与华盛顿、杰斐逊、林肯并列；又为何在 2022 年要把他的骑马铜像从纽约自然历史博物馆门前移走？</p>\n<p>全卷分为三章。第一章追问罗斯福如何重新定义了&quot;总统&quot;这个职位本身——他被广泛称为&quot;第一位现代总统&quot;，把白宫从被动的行政机关变成了塑造民意、主动立法的&quot;讲坛&quot;，并以&quot;新国家主义&quot;为后来罗斯福新政、肯尼迪新边疆乃至林登·约翰逊伟大社会铺设了思想轨道。</p>\n<p>第二章梳理那些至今仍在运转的制度遗产：被他从纸面法律激活的反垄断与监管国家、覆盖两亿三千万英亩的公共土地体系、以及把美国正式推上世界舞台的强权外交。这些遗产不是抽象口号，而是今天仍在影响每个美国人生活的具体机构与法律。</p>\n<p>第三章则进入最尖锐的地带：史学界的排名共识与持续修正，以及围绕种族观念、帝国主义与纪念物的当代清算。罗斯福长期稳居&quot;最伟大总统&quot;前五，但他对优生学的支持、对菲律宾的征服、以及那座暗含种族等级秩序的铜像，都使得&quot;如何纪念他&quot;成为二十一世纪美国公共记忆争论的典型样本。</p>\n<p>阅读本卷，应当带着一种历史的克制：既不把罗斯福简化为进步英雄，也不把他降格为时代的罪人。一个更诚实的目标，是理解他为何同时是这两者，以及一个民族如何与自己复杂的伟人共处。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"reshaping-the-presidency","title":"重塑总统职位与现代政治","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reshaping-the-presidency","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-first-modern-president","title":"第一位现代总统","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reshaping-the-presidency/the-first-modern-president"},{"seq":2,"slug":"bully-pulpit-and-public-leadership","title":"讲坛：舆论领导力的发明","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reshaping-the-presidency/bully-pulpit-and-public-leadership"},{"seq":3,"slug":"new-nationalism-and-the-welfare-state","title":"新国家主义与福利国家的雏形","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reshaping-the-presidency/new-nationalism-and-the-welfare-state"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"enduring-institutional-legacy","title":"持久的制度遗产","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/enduring-institutional-legacy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"conservation-and-the-public-lands","title":"自然保护与公共土地体系","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/enduring-institutional-legacy/conservation-and-the-public-lands"},{"seq":2,"slug":"regulatory-state-and-progressive-reform","title":"监管国家与进步主义改革","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/enduring-institutional-legacy/regulatory-state-and-progressive-reform"},{"seq":3,"slug":"american-power-on-the-world-stage","title":"美国登上世界舞台","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/enduring-institutional-legacy/american-power-on-the-world-stage"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"reputation-and-reassessment","title":"声誉、争议与再评价","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reputation-and-reassessment","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"presidential-rankings-and-historiography","title":"总统排名与史学评价","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reputation-and-reassessment/presidential-rankings-and-historiography"},{"seq":2,"slug":"race-imperialism-and-the-monuments-debate","title":"种族、帝国主义与纪念物之争","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-legacy/reputation-and-reassessment/race-imperialism-and-the-monuments-debate"}]}]}